{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedCornersAlong","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedCornersAlong","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.SchenstedWordSurjectivity"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_uninsertSteps_insertWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_uninsertSteps_insertWord","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCornersAlong.lean#L121-L131","doc":"**Brick 14's hypotheses are satisfiable.** Both discharged, for every word.\n\nThe conclusion is weaker than brick 3's `uninsertSteps_insertWord` (which pins the recovered word\non the nose, not merely its insertion tableau), and that is the point: this is a consistency check\non brick 14, not a new result about `insertWord`. What it buys is that\n`insertWord_uninsertSteps` is a theorem with inhabited hypotheses. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsertSteps_insertWord_fst","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.uninsertSteps_insertWord_fst","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCornersAlong.lean#L116-L119","doc":"The emptying condition, at the empty starting tableau — brick 3, read off its first component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_insertWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_insertWord","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCornersAlong.lean#L112-L114","doc":"The corner condition, at the empty starting tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_noEmptyRows","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insertWord_noEmptyRows","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCornersAlong.lean#L97-L110","doc":"**No insertion tableau has an empty row.** The fold of brick 2's `insert_noEmptyRows`.\n\n`insertWord_rowsSorted` and `insertWord_colStrict` are both in `SchenstedInsertion`, but this third\none is not: `insert_noEmptyRows` is defined downstream, in `SchenstedReverseCascade`, so the fold\nwas never taken. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_rowIndices","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.cornersAlong_rowIndices","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCornersAlong.lean#L82-L95","doc":"**Every insertion-built run removes corners.** The corner condition at step `k` is checked\nagainst the tableau after the later steps are undone, which brick 3's `uninsertSteps_foldl` says is\nthe tableau after `k + 1` insertions — so it is exactly `insert_isCorner`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_isCorner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.insert_isCorner","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCornersAlong.lean#L59-L80","doc":"**Insertion always creates a corner.** The cell `insert T x` adds sits at the end of its row\nwith the row below strictly shorter.\n\nThe no-bump case is the whole content: the row grows from `L - 1` to `L`, and `ColStrict` had\nalready bounded the row below by `L - 1`. Had the row below been as long, the tableau we started\nfrom would not have been a Young shape. The bumping case is the recursion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.headD_tail_length_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.Schensted.headD_tail_length_le","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/SchenstedCornersAlong.lean#L52-L57","doc":"The first row of a column-strict tableau bounds the second. ","signatureChunk":0}]}